{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.QuantumIntBarSymmetric","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.QuantumIntBarSymmetric","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.StandardModel.ThetaQcdFramingCp"],"declarations":10,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.QuantumIntBarSymmetric.parity_gate_admits_all_quantumInt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.QuantumIntBarSymmetric.parity_gate_admits_all_quantumInt","kind":"theorem","line":125,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QuantumIntBarSymmetric.lean#L125-L130","doc":"Restated as the parity statement the S1 argument uses: the bar-parity gate\nadmits `[n]_q` for **every** `n`, so it cannot distinguish between them. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.QuantumIntBarSymmetric.quantumInt_isCPEven","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.QuantumIntBarSymmetric.quantumInt_isCPEven","kind":"theorem","line":112,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QuantumIntBarSymmetric.lean#L112-L123","doc":"**Every symmetric q-integer is bar-symmetric.**\n\nBoth numerator and denominator are bar-anti-symmetric; the two signs cancel\nin the quotient.  Holds for all `n : ℕ` with no further hypotheses beyond\n`bar q = q⁻¹` and a nonvanishing denominator. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.QuantumIntBarSymmetric.denominator_bar_antisymmetric","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.QuantumIntBarSymmetric.denominator_bar_antisymmetric","kind":"theorem","line":106,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QuantumIntBarSymmetric.lean#L106-L110","doc":"The denominator `q - q⁻¹` is bar-**anti**-symmetric. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.QuantumIntBarSymmetric.numerator_bar_antisymmetric","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.QuantumIntBarSymmetric.numerator_bar_antisymmetric","kind":"theorem","line":96,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QuantumIntBarSymmetric.lean#L96-L104","doc":"The numerator `qⁿ - q⁻ⁿ` is bar-**anti**-symmetric, for every `n`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.QuantumIntBarSymmetric.quantumInt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.QuantumIntBarSymmetric.quantumInt","kind":"def","line":92,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QuantumIntBarSymmetric.lean#L92-L94","doc":"The **symmetric** q-integer `[n]_q = (qⁿ - q⁻ⁿ)/(q - q⁻¹)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.QuantumIntBarSymmetric.bar_inv_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.QuantumIntBarSymmetric.bar_inv_eq","kind":"theorem","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QuantumIntBarSymmetric.lean#L85-L90","doc":"The bar action on the substrate parameter is an involution on `q`:\n`bar q = q⁻¹` forces `bar q⁻¹ = q`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.QuantumIntBarSymmetric.bar_inv'","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.QuantumIntBarSymmetric.bar_inv'","kind":"theorem","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QuantumIntBarSymmetric.lean#L70-L83","doc":"`bar` commutes with inversion on nonzero elements: from `bar_mul` and\n`bar_one`, `bar x * bar x⁻¹ = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.QuantumIntBarSymmetric.bar_sub'","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.QuantumIntBarSymmetric.bar_sub'","kind":"theorem","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QuantumIntBarSymmetric.lean#L60-L63","doc":"`bar` commutes with subtraction. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.QuantumIntBarSymmetric.bar_neg'","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.QuantumIntBarSymmetric.bar_neg'","kind":"theorem","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QuantumIntBarSymmetric.lean#L54-L58","doc":"`bar` is additive-inverse preserving. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.QuantumIntBarSymmetric.bar_zero'","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.QuantumIntBarSymmetric.bar_zero'","kind":"theorem","line":46,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QuantumIntBarSymmetric.lean#L46-L52","doc":"`bar 0 = 0`, from additivity alone. ","signatureChunk":0}]}